{% comment %}
  A sleeve of film the visitor scrolls through, frame by frame.

  The photographs sit in the black band of 35mm strips and the two scanner
  buttons advance them one frame at a time. Nothing else on the site looks
  like this, which is the point — it is the lab showing work the way the lab
  sees it, on the light table.

  ADDING PHOTOGRAPHS
  Everything is managed in the theme editor. Each Frame block is one
  photograph, with the photographer's name and a link — usually to their
  Instagram or website, so the credit goes somewhere. Blocks without an image
  are skipped, so a half-filled block never shows as a gap.

  STRIPS
  Frames are cut into strips of "Frames per strip", the way negatives come
  back in a sleeve, and a new strip starts whenever one fills. Adding
  photographs therefore makes the sheet taller rather than one strip ever
  longer. All strips live inside a single scroll container so they move
  together — see .cfl-ticker__sheet in cfl-components.css for why.

  HOW IT SCROLLS
  This is the theme's own <slider-component> (assets/global.js), not a bespoke
  scroller. It tracks position, watches for resize, disables the buttons at
  each end and moves exactly one frame per click; underneath it is a native
  overflow-x container, so trackpad, touch swipe and arrow keys all work
  without any code here.

  The contract with <slider-component> is naming: the scroll container's id
  must start with "Slider-", frames it measures must have ids starting
  "Slide-", and the buttons must be name="previous" and name="next". Rename
  any of those and the film silently stops responding.

  Only frames in the FIRST strip get a Slide- id. The component decides when
  to disable the next button by checking whether the last Slide- is visible,
  and the first strip is always the longest — it fills before a second one
  starts. Numbering every frame would make the last one a frame in a short
  final strip, and the button would disable while the top strip still had
  photographs off screen.

  HOW IT SCALES
  Entirely in CSS, off a single height variable, using multipliers measured
  from the strip artwork. See the cfl-film-ticker block in cfl-components.css
  — the geometry is explained there, and it is the only place those numbers
  should be edited.
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'cfl-components.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- style -%}
  .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
    padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
    padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
      padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;
      padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;
    }
  }
{%- endstyle -%}

{%- liquid
  assign per_strip = section.settings.frames_per_strip

  assign photo_count = 0
  for block in section.blocks
    if block.type == 'frame' and block.settings.image != blank
      assign photo_count = photo_count | plus: 1
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    A strip with one photograph on it is not a strip, and slider-component
    needs two frames before it will measure a step at all — below two it
    returns without binding the buttons, leaving them inert. So below two this
    renders nothing rather than something broken.
  endcomment
-%}

{%- if photo_count >= 2 -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Deliberately not .page-width. The strips are meant to run off both edges of
    the screen; boxing them into the content column would put a hard cut end on
    film that is supposed to continue past the frame.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="cfl-ticker-section color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} gradient section-{{ section.id }}-padding">
    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <h2 class="cfl-section-heading {{ section.settings.heading_size }}">
        {{- section.settings.heading | escape -}}
      </h2>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.intro != blank -%}
      <p class="cfl-section-intro cfl-ticker-section__intro">{{ section.settings.intro | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    <slider-component
      class="cfl-ticker"
      style="--cfl-ticker-max-h: {{ section.settings.strip_height }}rem;"
    >
      <div
        id="Slider-{{ section.id }}"
        class="cfl-ticker__viewport"
        tabindex="0"
        role="group"
        aria-label="{{ section.settings.heading | default: 'Film gallery' | escape }}, scrollable film strips"
      >
        <div class="cfl-ticker__sheet">
          {%- assign n = 0 -%}
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- if block.type == 'frame' and block.settings.image != blank -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign position_in_strip = n | modulo: per_strip

                assign credit = block.settings.photographer | strip
                assign link = block.settings.link

                assign alt = block.settings.alt | strip
                if alt == blank and credit != blank
                  assign alt = 'Photograph by ' | append: credit
                endif

                comment
                  Links typed as a full address are someone else's site — the
                  photographer's — and open in a new tab so the visitor does not
                  lose the store. Links picked from the store's own pages come
                  through as relative paths and open in place.
                endcomment
                assign external = false
                if link contains '://'
                  assign external = true
                endif
              -%}

              {%- if position_in_strip == 0 -%}
                <ul class="cfl-ticker__film" role="list">
              {%- endif -%}

              <li
                {% if n < per_strip %}
                  id="Slide-{{ section.id }}-{{ n | plus: 1 }}"
                {% endif %}
                class="cfl-ticker__frame"
                {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
              >
                {%- if link != blank -%}
                  <a
                    class="cfl-ticker__photo"
                    href="{{ link }}"
                    {% if external %}
                      target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                    {% endif %}
                    {% if alt == blank %}
                      aria-label="View photograph"
                    {% endif %}
                  >
                {%- else -%}
                  <div class="cfl-ticker__photo">
                {%- endif -%}

                {{
                  block.settings.image
                  | image_url: width: 900
                  | image_tag:
                    loading: 'lazy',
                    widths: '300, 450, 600, 900',
                    sizes: '38rem',
                    alt: alt
                }}

                {%- if credit != blank -%}
                  <span class="cfl-ticker__credit">
                    {%- comment -%}
                      Hidden from screen readers: the image's alt text already
                      names the photographer, and reading it twice in a row is
                      noise.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    <span aria-hidden="true">Photo by {{ credit | escape }}{% if external %} ↗{% endif %}</span>
                  </span>
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- if link != blank -%}
                  {%- if external -%}
                    <span class="visually-hidden">(opens in a new tab)</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  </a>
                {%- else -%}
                  </div>
                {%- endif -%}
              </li>

              {%- assign n = n | plus: 1 -%}
              {%- assign strip_filled = n | modulo: per_strip -%}
              {%- if strip_filled == 0 or n == photo_count -%}
                </ul>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cfl-ticker__controls">
        <button
          type="button"
          name="previous"
          class="cfl-ticker__button"
          aria-controls="Slider-{{ section.id }}"
          aria-label="Previous frame"
        >
          <img
            src="{{ section.settings.button_left | default: 'https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0585/6093/8038/files/ScannerButtonLeft.png?v=1754933785' }}"
            alt=""
            width="500"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
          >
        </button>

        <button
          type="button"
          name="next"
          class="cfl-ticker__button"
          aria-controls="Slider-{{ section.id }}"
          aria-label="Next frame"
        >
          <img
            src="{{ section.settings.button_right | default: 'https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0585/6093/8038/files/ScannerButtonRight.png?v=1754933786' }}"
            alt=""
            width="500"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
          >
        </button>
      </div>
    </slider-component>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Film ticker",
  "class": "section",
  "tag": "section",
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header", "footer"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Photographs laid into 35mm film strips, scrolled with the two scanner buttons. Add a Frame block for each photograph. Needs at least two frames with images before it appears."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Landscapes in Emulsion"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "heading_size",
      "label": "Heading size",
      "options": [
        { "value": "h2", "label": "Small" },
        { "value": "h1", "label": "Medium" },
        { "value": "h0", "label": "Large" }
      ],
      "default": "h1"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "intro",
      "label": "Intro line",
      "info": "Optional. A line of context under the heading."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "frames_per_strip",
      "label": "Frames per strip",
      "info": "When a strip is full, the next photograph starts a new strip below it. Real 35mm negatives come back cut into strips of 6.",
      "min": 3,
      "max": 12,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 6
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "strip_height",
      "label": "Strip height on desktop",
      "info": "The whole component scales from this — frame size and spacing follow it. Phones size themselves to the screen.",
      "min": 24,
      "max": 48,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "rem",
      "default": 36
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Buttons"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Leave blank to use the scanner buttons already on the store's CDN."
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "button_left",
      "label": "Left button image URL"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "button_right",
      "label": "Right button image URL"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "Color scheme",
      "default": "background-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Section padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Padding top",
      "default": 36
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Padding bottom",
      "default": 36
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "name": "Frame",
      "limit": 50,
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "image_picker",
          "id": "image",
          "label": "Photograph"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "photographer",
          "label": "Photographer",
          "info": "Shown on the photograph as \"Photo by …\". Leave blank to show no credit."
        },
        {
          "type": "url",
          "id": "link",
          "label": "Link",
          "info": "Where the photograph goes when clicked — the photographer's Instagram or website. Links to other sites open in a new tab."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "alt",
          "label": "Description",
          "info": "For screen readers and search. Name what is in the frame. If blank, \"Photograph by\" and the photographer's name is used."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Film ticker"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
